// pond/jobs — shape types.
//
// Pattern 5 (shape types, pure data, no flow). Per CONTRACTS.md
// the public data surface is:
//
//   type Job       { kind, payload, attempt, max_attempts }
//   type JobResult { ok, detail }
//   type JobError  { kind, detail }
//
// All three are pure-data records returnable from fns by value.
// `JobError` is the `fallible(JobError)` payload across the Queue
// member-fn surface (enqueue / dequeue / ack / fail — queue.hl).
// `JobResult` is what a JobHandler returns per invocation; the
// worker branches on `.ok` to choose ack-vs-fail. `Job` is the row
// shape stored in the SQLite-backed queue table.
//
// Status (2026-06-12): UNBLOCKED — pond/sqlite is a real @ffi
// driver and this lib's queue ops run real SQL. See FRICTION.log
// for the historical stub-era entries.

// Job — one queued unit of work as it lives on the wire / in
// the queue table.
//
// `id` is the queue row id (AUTOINCREMENT primary key), stamped by
// `dequeue()` so the worker can issue `ack(id)` / `fail(id, retry)`
// for the row it claimed. **Deviation from CONTRACTS.md** (which
// omits `id` — see FRICTION.log item 6): without it the contract's
// own ack/fail surface is uncallable from a worker. 0 = "not from
// the queue" (e.g. a hand-built Job).
//
// `kind` is a free-text discriminator the handler dispatches on
// (e.g. "send_email", "rebuild_index"). `payload` carries the
// per-job arguments as an opaque String (consumers serialize their
// own per-kind payload format — JSON, tab-separated, whatever).
// `attempt` starts at 0 on enqueue and increments on every retry;
// `max_attempts` caps the attempt count (after which a failing job
// goes to the dead-letter row state). Both are stored on the row so
// the worker computes the retry/dead-letter decision without
// re-reading the queue schema.
//
// v0 row-shape caveat: `kind` must not contain tab or newline
// (dequeue parses the tab-separated row). `payload` is parsed as
// the row remainder so embedded TABS are safe, but a NEWLINE in
// the payload is not.
type Job {
    id: Int = 0;
    kind: String = "";
    payload: String = "";
    attempt: Int = 0;
    max_attempts: Int = 3;
}

// JobResult — what a JobHandler returns per invocation.
//
// `ok = true` → the worker acks the row (marks done).
// `ok = false` → the worker calls `fail(job_id, retry: ...)`
// where `retry` is `attempt + 1 < max_attempts`. `detail` is a
// short human-readable diagnostic.
type JobResult {
    ok: Bool = false;
    detail: String = "";
}

// JobError — fallible(JobError) payload across the queue surface.
//
// `kind` is one of:
//   "empty"        — `dequeue()` found no ready row to claim (idle).
//   "db"           — the underlying sqlite call failed; `detail`
//                    carries the wrapped DbError kind + detail.
//   "not_found"    — `ack(id)` / `fail(id, _)` found no in_flight
//                    row with that id (already acked, never
//                    claimed, or never enqueued).
// `detail` is the human-readable explanation suitable for log
// emission.
type JobError {
    kind: String = "";
    detail: String = "";
}
